  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole. The project began with a kickoff on July 15th and an initial call for AI-driven data visualization ideas by July 20th. Initial findings presented on August 5th suggested a 20% efficiency increase. The team expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th. Following the design phase, the project moved to development under lead developer Omar Jensen. A significant milestone was reached with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. A training budget of $15,000 was approved for the coding team and project managers. Finally, feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
